  "bun": {
    "why": "Bun formats %p in array-table titles with multi-line pretty-format and [Function: noop], where Jest uses the compact form. Bun 1.4.2 doesn't format .each titles: $name stays as written, in its console output as well as its report. Bun misreads tagged-template .each tables: it runs more rows than written, with undefined values, so an assertion comparing two cells compares undefined with undefined and passes.",
    "verdicts": {
      "__tests__/pretty.test.js": {
        "array › [\n  {\n    foo: {\n      bar: \"baz\",\n    },\n  }\n] == [\n  {\n    foo: {\n      bar: \"baz\",\n    },\n  }\n]": [
          null,
          "pass"
        ],
